    {'para': "**106.** It will be the practice everywhere in this work to separate independent words in transliteration, but not in the *devanāgarī* text; and if an initial vowel of a following word has coalesced with a final of the preceding, this will be indicated by an apostrophe — single if the initial vowel be the shorter, double if it be the longer, of the two different initials which in every case of combination yield the same result. To aid the beginner, a point will sometimes be placed, in the *devanāgarī*, under a long vowel formed by two coalescing vowels; thus, ⟨agninā 'rīṇām⟩."},
