    {'para': '∗ Final ⟨m⟩ is commonly written as *anusvāra* if the following word begins with a consonant; but the Hindus pronounce it as ⟨m⟩ in such cases. At the end of a sentence *anusvāra* should not be written for ⟨m⟩, though this is a habit common in the MSS. Final radical ⟨m⟩, in internal combination, is assimilated to a following mute or spirant. In the former case it becomes the nasal of the same class with the mute; in the latter it becomes *anusvāra*. — Final radical ⟨n⟩, in internal combination, becomes *anusvāra* before a sibilant.'},
